{
  "description": "issue #679 (SP7) + issue #847: the documented way to home EVERY addressed turtle is `each [ clear_screen ]`, and this pins it. Where a bare `clear_screen` under `tell [ :a :b ]` emits ONE `clear` and homes only the current turtle (clear-screen-multi-turtle-homes-current; issue #738 tracks whether that should change), `each` runs the command once per addressed turtle, so each turtle gets its own canvas clear AND its own issue #847 homing triple - `move` ([0 10] -> [0 0], reporting the pre-reset heading 45) then `turn` (45 -> 0) then `clear`, all three stamped with that turtle's `turtle_id`. No `draw-segment` accompanies either homing move even though both pens are down: the same instruction goes on to clear the drawing (spec/rendering.md:36 describes what a pen-down move contributes to the RETAINED SCENE, and :148's \"Clear operations\" row fixes `clear_screen`'s contribution at *cleared*; escalated to the maintainer as issue #858). The trailing `each` proves the outcome rather than just the events - BOTH turtles report [0 0] and heading 0, unlike the single-`clear_screen` fixture where :b is left at [0 10] heading 45. Every change of the addressed set - the `tell`, each `each` iteration, and each restoration - emits an addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }` (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:191).",
